-- title:
--   Frobenius image in M/pM is free of rank d
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$ (a field with `CharP k p` and `PerfectRing k p`), let $d$ be a natural number, and let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $k$: a $d$-tuple of power series in the $2d$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, with linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each group of variables, and satisfying the associativity identity; assume moreover `Φ.IsComm`, i.e. each component is invariant under swapping the two groups of variables. Assume the finite-height hypothesis `hfin`: the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the $d$ components of `Φ.nthSeries p`, the $p$-fold iterate $[p]_\Phi$ obtained from `nthSeries` by repeatedly substituting into $\Phi$, is a finite $k$-module. Write $M$ for `CartierModule p Φ`, whose elements are $d$-tuples of power series in countably many variables with zero constant terms compatible with the Witt addition law `addFam` and $\Phi$, and let `frobenius` be precomposition with the Verschiebung substitution `verFam`. The conclusion asserts that the $W(k)/pW(k)$-submodule of $M/(p\cdot M)$ spanned by the classes of the elements $Ff$, $f\in M$, admits a basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$.
--
--   This is the Frobenius-twisted form of Cartier's structure theorem: for a commutative formal group law of finite height and dimension $d$ over a perfect field, the image of $F$ in $M/pM$ is free of rank $d$ over $W(k)/pW(k)\cong k$, reflecting $F\colon M/VM\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }FM/pM$ and $\dim_k M/VM=\dim\Phi$. It feeds the computations of $M/pM$ and of its Frobenius quotient used in the determination of the rank of the Cartier–Dieudonné module when the height is $p^h$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_CartierModule_nonempty_basis_span_frobenius_of_finite_quotient.lean

